Optional real-input Lean certification benchmark
================================================

LassoRanker is manual-only. It is not part of PR CI, scheduled/nightly builds,
or the fast Lean integration corpus. A measured run took about 109 seconds
to produce the certificate and 830 seconds to check an approximately 89 MB
Lean proof; hosted-runner performance has not been established.

lra_lassoranker.smt2 is an unchanged copy of:

  formulas/LassoRanker-CooperatingT2-efegp.t2.c_Iteration1_Lasso_3-pieceTemplate.smt2

from jreeves3/SMT-Skeleton-Check at commit
acfcc71fc920cf02122917d63599a71301d57296:

  https://github.com/jreeves3/SMT-Skeleton-Check/blob/acfcc71fc920cf02122917d63599a71301d57296/formulas/LassoRanker-CooperatingT2-efegp.t2.c_Iteration1_Lasso_3-pieceTemplate.smt2

The upstream MIT license is preserved in LICENSE. The input also retains its
original Ultimate LassoRanker attribution and benchmark-generation metadata.

SHA-256:
  98d82ddb9c67d108fb2c5f0725924d6277ab8faee96adbc3d894be53c36be6a2

The input declares QF_LRA and has 1,463 Real variables and 105 assertions.
Its expected result is unsat. No options, assertions, declarations, or queries
have been removed or rewritten. Upstream whitespace in the attribution block
is also preserved so the file remains byte-for-byte identical.

Unlike the small parent-directory fixtures, this input has a large search
log. Certification needs the Z3 checkout's dependency-directed log reduction,
EUF congruence-annotation support, and corrected native proof trimmer.
The original log and its reduced dependency core are both retained; native
trimming is not a trusted checker, and every retained inference must produce
a Lean-checkable proof connected to the original assertions.

To opt in explicitly, run from the z3test checkout:

  python3 scripts/proofs/proof_matrix.py \
    --z3 /path/to/z3/build/z3 --z3-source /path/to/z3 \
    --lean --cells smt-clause-log-nopp --timeout 300 --lean-timeout 1800 \
    --lean-artifacts /tmp/lra-real-artifacts --out /tmp/lra-real.jsonl \
    regressions/proofs/lean/real/lra_lassoranker.smt2

The manual command still requires lean-verified; a timeout, unsupported
inference, or rejected proof is not a passing result. It does not raise the
default budgets of other matrix runs.

trim_satisfied_clause.proof is the minimized proof-trimming regression:
with p true and q false, (p or q or r) is already satisfied and must not
propagate r. The real contradiction uses the later assumption (not p).
This tiny regression, unlike the full LassoRanker benchmark, is checked by
the regular integration suite.
